 "finding": [
  "Not a plain alphabet writing Latin or Italian: its next-sign entropy is 2.17 bits, where a Latin herbal, Macer's verse and Italian recipes give 2.92 to 3.41.",
  "Not a syllabary like Linear B: the signs fall into clear columns, but the signs that swap at the ends of word families all join one row, a single set of endings.",
  "Closest to a cipher in its letters, furthest in its order: Greshko's Naibbe cipher matches its entropy (2.08) but has none of its word repeats, one-sign neighbours, line-edge signs or paragraph-opening gallows."
